          "date": "2026-10-05 14:55:28.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20791 efalnd: Refresh receive connection on arrival",
        "message": "LU-20791 efalnd: Refresh receive connection on arrival\n\nThe receive path looked up the responder connection only when a message\nwas delivered from LNet. Messages that never reach delivery,\ncompletions, connection establishment and drops, did not refresh the\nconnection use time, so a busy responder connection could look idle and\nbe reaped.\n\nMove the lookup to the point where a received buffer is first handled\nand stash the connection on the buffer, so delivery reuses it. The use\ntime is now refreshed on every arriving message, and a request with no\nconnection is rejected before it is handed to LNet.\n\nThe reference taken at arrival is held until the message is done, so it\nalso keeps the connection alive across the gap between arrival and\ndelivery, during which a request can sit parked, preventing the daemon\nfrom reaping it out from under the delivery callback. It is released\nwhere the message is handled, or in the delivery callback for requests\npassed up to LNet.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nChange-Id: Iedd6eeee7951f8643992cefa69fc0010c006aef2\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
